        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Patient gained 6kg since starting mirtazapine 6 weeks ago. BP elevated to 168/98 (was 135/80). Mirtazapine commonly causes weight gain and increased appetite. Weight gain worsens hypertension and increases cardiac risk post-MI. Need to increase BP meds but limited options: 1) Can't use diltiazem (caused rhabdomyolysis with statin), 2) Already on metoprolol and lisinopril, 3) Could add amlodipine but may cause edema, 4) Could add HCTZ but may worsen gout (patient has history). Added amlodipine 5mg. Also patient now reporting dizziness (orthostatic hypotension from metoprolol?) and fatigue. Labs show worsening renal function (Cr 2.1, eGFR 28). Multiple medication adverse effects creating cascade of problems.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
